 {"kind": "text", "text": "common queries", "bbox": {"x": 972.6226791034869, "y": 564.1037155804108, "width": 174.97754911375964, "height": 29.603692710399628}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "included vaccination safety/efficacy in the setting of various comorbidities, including autoimmune disease, history of venous or arterial thrombosis, and immunodeficiency.", "bbox": {"x": 649.8913225380637, "y": 588.6697772143585, "width": 499.9784597038248, "height": 113.92502192258827}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "An important category of eConsult involved possible reaction to a first dose of the COVID-19 vaccine. Commonly reported concerns included possible IgE-mediated response, delayed skin rashes, and neurologic symptoms such as paresthesia post immunization. This comprised a significant number of eConsults, but was likely underrepresented as a whole given rising numbers of first doses rates administered in the latter months of our study [20).", "bbox": {"x": 653.757452773552, "y": 684.8601635063593, "width": 507.2697866995913, "height": 243.21265211105353}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "The Consult process did effectively alter the planned clinical path for a significant number of patients studied.", "bbox": {"x": 662.9598915537953, "y": 912.4575763111999, "width": 499.5487130396372, "height": 89.38632469177236}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "reviewed", "bbox": {"x": 1068.9318811708447, "y": 962.1999996462501, "width": 92.02724795640333, "height": 21.224999999999923}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "(360/499) were answered by specialist electronically without requirement for external resources or referral to other specialty (Table 3). After completion of consultation, only a small percentage of eConsult responses recommended in-person allergy assessment or another specialist referral. From a PCP perspective (Table 4), although in-person referral was initially considered in 276/499 cases, 220 of the 276 eConsults (79.7%) were ultimately managed without an in-person referral. These rates are higher than those previously documented with other specialties; 38% in a similar study of rheumatology Consults and 66% in a study of hematology eConsults [12-14]. Interestingly, PCPs used the Consult service for 181 patients when they hadn't intended to refer a patient in the first place, and 9 of those Consults lead to formal in-person consultation.", "bbox": {"x": 664.8437628834602, "y": 988.3023583111806, "width": 512.406547442444, "height": 437.994154214859}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Discussion", "bbox": {"x": 683.1253404224797, "y": 1453.9124999634053, "width": 109.72479564032686, "height": 21.224999999999923}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Summary & explanation", "bbox": {"x": 682.5364457585166, "y": 1473.672227577723, "width": 206.55522004005377, "height": 29.75300925970084}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Our study is the first of its kind to describe an eConsult platform as it pertains to clinical questions surrounding", "bbox": {"x": 684.8108083653275, "y": 1486.314844051143, "width": 495.52531318768496, "height": 68.67211818695068}}], "ms": 452.102375}